PR #65 is merged and CI-green, but Codex review finds Gates 0–2 incomplete. No native run is authorized.

::code-comment{title="[P1] Tool probe never invokes either codec" body="probe_codec_floor claims to encode and decode a probe, but it only checks that the executable exists and returns verified=True. This does not establish that preset 0/slower is accepted, produces a non-empty bitstream, or decodes correctly." file="/home/itec/emanuele/pointstream/experiments/tier/gate_a_tools.py" start=107 end=126 priority=1}

::code-comment{title="[P1] Required controls are not executed" body="run_gate_a_controls executes only metric calibration and the shuffled-frame null. The required object-stream-off and conventional-fallback controls are absent, even though a standalone fallback checker exists above." file="/home/itec/emanuele/pointstream/experiments/tier/gate_a_controls.py" start=107 end=123 priority=1}

::code-comment{title="[P1] Driver has no native execution path" body="The driver can only produce dry-run metadata; without --dry-run, main prints that authorization is required and exits. There is no bounded runner for AV1/VVC curves, PointStream rungs, checkpoints, budget accounting, adaptive duration gates, or adjudication." file="/home/itec/emanuele/pointstream/experiments/tier/gate_a_long_context.py" start=208 end=270 priority=1}

::code-comment{title="[P1] Pre-run bounds do not implement the frozen brief" body="These narrow rung-specific values replace the approved broad instrument-alarm bounds and assume bytes scale linearly with duration—the amortisation behavior Gate A exists to measure. Required BD-rate, shape, clock, monotonicity, access-pattern, raw-byte ceiling, and late-frame bounds are missing." file="/home/itec/emanuele/pointstream/experiments/tier/gate_a_long_context.py" start=88 end=125 priority=1}

::code-comment{title="[P1] Measurement identity is incomplete" body="The identity omits the implementation commit, clean/dirty state and dirty-file hashes, driver/metric/wrapper hashes, colour convention, native dimensions, eligibility labels, binary identities, and explicit prefix shape/dtype. Consequently it cannot enforce the measurement identity frozen in Gate 0." file="/home/itec/emanuele/pointstream/experiments/tier/gate_a_identity.py" start=125 end=157 priority=1}

Additional findings:

- The claimed C1 “regression” is a hard-coded BP56 ledger assertion; it does not run the merged implementation or prove byte-identical output.
- The “independent client” test passes an already decoded `BackgroundModelView`, not transmitted payload bytes, and tests no foreground placements. It therefore does not establish the required byte-only client boundary.
- Only 48/96/192-frame source identities exist. The reported reason for excluding 384 frames changes the original experiment ceiling and must be formally adjudicated.
- The existing uncommitted readiness-document edit remains untouched.

Required next step: a repair PR implementing the actual codec probe, full controls, complete identity/bounds, genuine byte-only client regression, and bounded native execution/checkpoint/budget machinery. After that, Codex should review a fresh 48-frame dry-run artifact before authorizing even the first native control point.
